msgid "Category of existing patrons"
msgstr ""

msgid "Do not change the category of patrons that already exist"
msgstr ""

msgid "When ticked, the category is only set for new patrons. Existing patrons keep the category they have, so categories that are handled in Koha are not overwritten by the default category."
msgstr ""

msgid "Contact details"
msgstr ""

msgid "Keep existing contact details when IST has no value"
msgstr ""

msgid "When ticked, an empty e-mail, phone, mobile or address from IST never replaces a value the patron already has in Koha. Patrons missing these details in IST are still imported."
msgstr ""

msgid "missing in Koha"
msgstr ""

msgid "Category rules"
msgstr ""

msgid "A rule has one or more conditions and an action: a Koha category, or do not import. Conditions in one rule must all be true. Several values in one condition mean any of them. Rules are tried in priority order (lowest number first) and the first rule that matches decides. When no rule matches, the default category is used."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use rules"
msgstr ""

msgid "Decide the patron category with the rules below instead of the roles mapping"
msgstr ""

msgid "When this is not ticked the rules are ignored and the roles mapping works as before. When ticked, the roles mapping and \"Exclude empty users, dutyRole\" are not used; use a rule with the condition role is empty instead."
msgstr ""

